{"event_type":"review","id":"414064055397894772edb698a7413760248281d4640885a96eb0046d3bb432d8","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T18:52:33Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1b74c6a5bb8819c7a47153e07fcf0a6d23d42b08dcc6ab76353b51ad243fc910","sha256":"1b74c6a5bb8819c7a47153e07fcf0a6d23d42b08dcc6ab76353b51ad243fc910"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6205ea904f0bad03db8684dfdd15e17791daae337f0b415f19f600ca788cab74","sha256":"6205ea904f0bad03db8684dfdd15e17791daae337f0b415f19f600ca788cab74"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/eda03b6fcabd15ddfb3ad74b188bfe128cdf00f77fb8e0328acd42e9bdb93296","sha256":"eda03b6fcabd15ddfb3ad74b188bfe128cdf00f77fb8e0328acd42e9bdb93296"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d845b445bc387f36d693e15b4eabf76e30263b3ac21ecc6f593ef9b1c9c03099","sha256":"d845b445bc387f36d693e15b4eabf76e30263b3ac21ecc6f593ef9b1c9c03099"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/69d54e9cc51644dfab27742ee9537c5136a8b59b8f80e4aa0846e282dbc9834b","sha256":"69d54e9cc51644dfab27742ee9537c5136a8b59b8f80e4aa0846e282dbc9834b"}],"attempt_id":"49f515e553ff6224726bc8c255589da282ab2da9dfe652898e4a89aee41e5534:0:1","base":"7ccb77fe294695a0848994f888d1d04df1be6aac","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"dc8fcaebe4a7d7f834474a5ebe4be7836da30a33","body":"**Do not fall back to default policy when `cq.json` exists but cannot be read.**\n\nIn `src/ops/dev/ready.ts`, line 122 uses `.catch(() => null)`, so every read error is treated as \"no `cq.json`\". That includes `EACCES`, `EISDIR`, and `EIO`. When that happens, `policy` stays `undefined` and `assembleReadiness` falls back to `['critical', 'major']` and both reviewers. A repository that set stricter `review.blockingSeverities` would then get a READY verdict under looser rules, and nothing would show it. Only `ENOENT` should mean \"no config\". Any other read error should return `needs-human`.\n\n`src/ops/pr/open.ts`, lines 282-309, contains the same code. If you move it into one shared helper, `dev.ready` and `pr.open` cannot resolve policy differently.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed helper (call from both ops)</summary>\n\n```ts\n// e.g. src/ops/dev/internal/readinessPolicy.ts\nexport async function loadReadinessPolicy(\n  repoRoot: string,\n  op: string,\n): Promise<\n  | { ok: true; policy?: { reviewers: readonly string[]; blockingSeverities: readonly string[] } }\n  | { ok: false; reason: string }\n> {\n  let configText: string;\n  try {\n    configText = await readFile(join(repoRoot, 'cq.json'), 'utf8');\n  } catch (err) {\n    if ((err as { code?: unknown }).code === 'ENOENT') return { ok: true };\n    return { ok: false, reason: `${op}: cq.json could not be read — ${faultText(err)}` };\n  }\n  const parsed = parseCqConfig(configText, repoRoot);\n  if (!parsed.ok) return { ok: false, reason: `${op}: cq.json — ${parsed.reason}` };\n  // ...package name read + resolveCqConfigDefaults as today...\n}\n```\n</details>\n\nAs per path instructions: \"a public op maps failure onto the frozen taxonomy (status 'failed' with error), never a fabricated ok.\"","id":"a8663f6453412b7840f9170cbeed872250e59df472c87636306f05efa62d8dd5","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/dev/ready.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not fall back to default policy when `cq.json` exists but cannot be read."}],"head":"3cc38b31bbaf52a044218645560cf23f8723c40c","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"4567bd7e0fb9eed7887d97d5ed6dde0d8c2b551b","intervals":[[1,101]],"path":"src/ops/dev/index.ts"},{"blob":"dc8fcaebe4a7d7f834474a5ebe4be7836da30a33","intervals":[[1,158]],"path":"src/ops/dev/ready.ts"},{"blob":"e275514624c67ae166e5cb0574e2a8ef40597317","intervals":[[1,1263]],"path":"src/ops/dev/record.ts"},{"blob":"7305f80232f16052b9e73fbfa5e50e393f6a0bdf","intervals":[[1,1025]],"path":"src/ops/dev/review.ts"},{"blob":"018b46db388a3812daf6dc68c4a4113e229e52cf","intervals":[[1,480]],"path":"src/ops/pr/open.ts"}],"job_id":"49f515e553ff6224726bc8c255589da282ab2da9dfe652898e4a89aee41e5534:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"4567bd7e0fb9eed7887d97d5ed6dde0d8c2b551b","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/dev/index.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"dc8fcaebe4a7d7f834474a5ebe4be7836da30a33","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/dev/ready.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"e275514624c67ae166e5cb0574e2a8ef40597317","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/dev/record.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"7305f80232f16052b9e73fbfa5e50e393f6a0bdf","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/dev/review.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"018b46db388a3812daf6dc68c4a4113e229e52cf","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/pr/open.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"3aee477168e1da8e2aa232a98e80747d98da8f26f54f2a27e0c62d13e349d4b1","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"4567bd7e0fb9eed7887d97d5ed6dde0d8c2b551b","intervals":[[1,101]],"path":"src/ops/dev/index.ts"},{"blob":"dc8fcaebe4a7d7f834474a5ebe4be7836da30a33","intervals":[[1,158]],"path":"src/ops/dev/ready.ts"},{"blob":"e275514624c67ae166e5cb0574e2a8ef40597317","intervals":[[1,1263]],"path":"src/ops/dev/record.ts"},{"blob":"7305f80232f16052b9e73fbfa5e50